   {
    "name": "ship_progress",
    "description": "Track pull requests to production and show task progress in the bar above the prompt. The mod polls GitHub itself (PR CI → merged → main CI → deploys → checks) and wakes you when a stage fails or a PR goes live, so do not poll gh yourself for tracked PRs: call action \"status\" instead. Actions: track {pr}; untrack {pr}; annotate {pr, stage?, note}; add_step {pr, name, after?} adds a step you own to a PR; set_step {pr|list, name, state, note?} sets one of your steps; list_set {list, title, steps:[{name, state?, after?}]} declares a task list with no GitHub involvement; status {} returns every track and list as JSON. Watch only: it never merges, reruns or edits anything."
   }
